## Work

Three edits to `dashboard/__tests__/storytime-package-readalong-clips.test.ts` only:

1. N3 new case (Review A F1, the M5 text half): "a done sentence whose item text differs from the
   book sentence is made again". The case rewrites one provenance item's `text` to `<text> stale`
   (file and SHA-256 unchanged), runs the maker with `kinds: ['readalong']`, and asserts one call
   for the book text, the exact call line, no `kept` line for the stale sentence, the exact
   `kept` bytes of the other seven sentences, the final `sent:` line, and the rewritten item text.
2. N7 new case (Review A F2): "--kind all plans both kinds: the decodable kept lines and the
   read-along call list". The case runs `main` with `--kind all` on `phase12Tree()` with the fake
   voice, and asserts the exact stdout: 8 decodable `kept` lines, 8 read-along call lines with
   cumulative `sent`, `sent: 137`, `made: 8`, and that only read-along texts were called. No mmx
   call, no network.
3. N6 rename (Review A F3): the `it` name now reads "a fake that throws on call 2 gives 2 call
   lines and the failed sent line", which matches its body.

No other case changed. No production source changed. The Red 1 task marker stayed `[x]`; this
retry added sub-lines only.

